From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:16:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: offload 802.1ad tags to hardware

The software path pushes 802.1Q and 802.1ad tags alike, but the
hardware offload rule only knows 802.1Q. nf_flow_rule_match() drops an
802.1ad tag from the match, so with an 802.1ad outer tag the inner tag
becomes the vlan key and the driver cannot tell the outer VLAN apart.
nf_flow_rule_route_common() emits no pop for an 802.1ad tag, and on
push it takes an action entry without setting its id, which leaves a
FLOW_ACTION_ACCEPT where the push belongs.

Treat both TPIDs as a VLAN tag, as eth_type_vlan() does. The keys and
the push action already carry the TPID.

Fixes: 3e1b0c168f6c ("netfilter: flowtable: add vlan match offload support")
Fixes: efce49dfe6a8 ("netfilter: flowtable: add vlan pop action offload support")
Fixes: 17e52c0aaad7 ("netfilter: flowtable: support for FLOW_ACTION_PPPOE_PUSH")
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ static int nf_flow_rule_match(struct nf_
 	mask->meta.ingress_ifindex = 0xffffffff;
 
 	if (tuple->encap_num > 0 && !(tuple->in_vlan_ingress & BIT(0)) &&
-	    tuple->encap[0].proto == htons(ETH_P_8021Q)) {
+	    eth_type_vlan(tuple->encap[0].proto)) {
 		NF_FLOW_DISSECTOR(match, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_VLAN, vlan);
 		nf_flow_rule_vlan_match(&key->vlan, &mask->vlan,
 					tuple->encap[0].id,
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ static int nf_flow_rule_match(struct nf_
 	}
 
 	if (tuple->encap_num > 1 && !(tuple->in_vlan_ingress & BIT(1)) &&
-	    tuple->encap[1].proto == htons(ETH_P_8021Q)) {
+	    eth_type_vlan(tuple->encap[1].proto)) {
 		if (vlan_encap) {
 			NF_FLOW_DISSECTOR(match, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CVLAN,
 					  cvlan);
@@ -718,7 +718,7 @@ nf_flow_rule_route_common(struct net *ne
 		if (tuple->in_vlan_ingress & BIT(i))
 			continue;
 
-		if (tuple->encap[i].proto == htons(ETH_P_8021Q)) {
+		if (eth_type_vlan(tuple->encap[i].proto)) {
 			entry = flow_action_entry_next(flow_rule);
 			if (!entry)
 				return -1;
@@ -744,6 +744,7 @@ nf_flow_rule_route_common(struct net *ne
 			entry->pppoe.sid = other_tuple->encap[i].id;
 			break;
 		case htons(ETH_P_8021Q):
+		case htons(ETH_P_8021AD):
 			entry->id = FLOW_ACTION_VLAN_PUSH;
 			entry->vlan.vid = other_tuple->encap[i].id;
 			entry->vlan.proto = other_tuple->encap[i].proto;
